{
  "$comment": [
    "Product Line -> technology and type. The whole classification, in 43 rows.",
    "",
    "Global_Product_Hierarchy.xlsx classifies all 18,822 parts by Product Class,",
    "Product Line and Product Type. This file turns that into the two things the",
    "quoting tool needs: which price book a part belongs to, and what KIND of",
    "thing it is. Product Type is carried through separately as the model, for",
    "rule matching.",
    "",
    "WHY A FILE AND NOT CODE",
    "",
    "43 rows is a business decision, not logic. It is here so it can be corrected",
    "without a deployment, and every row says who decided it.",
    "",
    "WHY Product Class IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN",
    "",
    "'Coding' is four price books wearing one Product Class: Hi Res is piezo, IV",
    "is valve jet, Thermal Jet is thermal inkjet, and Engines are the printhead",
    "engines behind them. Mapping Class alone would put all four in one book.",
    "",
    "confidence 'confirmed' came from you. 'assumed' is my reading of the line",
    "name and needs a look - those are the rows to check first."
  ],
